<title>SINGAPORE: ANA seeks write-off of S$11.6 mln losses.</title>
<headline>ANA seeks write-off of S$11.6 mln losses.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>ANA Hotels Singapore Ltd said on Thursday it will hold an extraordinary general meeting of its shareholders on October 4 to seek approval to write off losses of S$11.62 million to be effected through an asset revaluation reserve and share premium account.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement it has also proposed new issue of 11.62 million ordinary shares at a price of S$1.00 each.</p>
<p>The proposed new issue is subject to approval by the shareholders.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
